WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:04.918 line:78%
Two humanoids get the same prompt, walk forward at 0.7 m/s,

2
00:00:04.918 --> 00:00:08.440 line:78%
and only the one on the right sees the stairs.

3
00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:18.086 line:78%
A behavior foundation model like BFM-Zero turns a reward,

4
00:00:18.086 --> 00:00:23.812 line:78%
a goal pose or a motion to follow into a prompt for one pre-trained humanoid policy.

5
00:00:23.812 --> 00:00:27.425 line:78%
Trained on flat ground and sensing only its own body,

6
00:00:27.425 --> 00:00:30.970 line:78%
it falls on stairs and boxes under the same prompts.

7
00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:37.290 line:78%
Perception should change how the robot carries out a prompt and leave what the prompt asks for unchanged.

8
00:00:39.400 --> 00:00:46.393 line:78%
SeeBFM continues BFM-Zero's pretraining on terrain with a height scan of the ground around the robot.

9
00:00:46.393 --> 00:00:51.793 line:78%
Every network reads the scan except the backward network, which turns rewards,

10
00:00:51.793 --> 00:00:54.285 line:78%
goal poses and motions into prompts,

11
00:00:54.285 --> 00:00:58.370 line:78%
so a prompt asks for the same body states on every terrain.

12
00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:04.934 line:78%
With the same six locomotion prompts,

13
00:01:04.934 --> 00:01:11.097 line:78%
SeeBFM crosses stairs going up in more than half of its attempts and boxes in two of five,

14
00:01:11.097 --> 00:01:13.220 line:78%
where BFM-Zero crosses neither.

15
00:01:15.400 --> 00:01:19.920 line:78%
On stairs the forward prompt slows down and lifts the swing foot over each step.

16
00:01:24.400 --> 00:01:28.520 line:78%
Crossing drops sharply when the scan is made level or left out of training.

17
00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:35.649 line:78%
Walking forward and turning carry over to terrain.

18
00:01:35.649 --> 00:01:40.522 line:78%
Walking sideways slows by more than half and walking backward nearly stops,

19
00:01:40.522 --> 00:01:46.890 line:78%
so SeeBFM stays on the edge of a box where the model trained without the scan steps off and falls.

20
00:01:49.400 --> 00:01:52.448 line:78%
Goal poses are prompted the same way on terrain,

21
00:01:52.448 --> 00:01:57.020 line:78%
where they end 2 to 4 cm further from their targets than on flat ground.

22
00:01:59.400 --> 00:02:01.470 line:78%
A real robot has no height scan,

23
00:02:01.470 --> 00:02:04.576 line:78%
so a depth student predicts it from two cameras.

24
00:02:04.576 --> 00:02:09.364 line:78%
We record SeeBFM's rollouts on terrain, render what each camera would see,

25
00:02:09.364 --> 00:02:15.510 line:78%
and train the student so the frozen policy acts on its prediction as it would on the true scan.

26
00:02:20.400 --> 00:02:24.318 line:78%
A language step turns a typed request into a motion prompt,

27
00:02:24.318 --> 00:02:30.360 line:78%
and SeeBFM carries out everyday requests in about half of its attempts on stairs and boxes.

28
00:02:37.400 --> 00:02:39.803 line:78%
All of these results are in simulation,

29
00:02:39.803 --> 00:02:43.500 line:78%
and tests on a G1 with the depth student are in preparation.

